Register VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D and VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D_DEBUG as vLLM env vars (vLLM 0.28.0).

The int4 multi-query 3D verify (patches/spec-decode-int4-kv-mq3d.patch) reads its
switch with os.environ.get inside the kernel module, so the value was outside
vLLM's registry and outside the torch.compile cache key. Harmless while the knob
was opt-in; a stale-graph hazard the moment single-user/alternative.sh defaults
it on and someone A/Bs INT4_MQ_3D=0 against 1 on a warm compile cache (review of
#93). Registered the way speed-knobs-envs.patch registers the other single-user
knobs; the kernel's own read is unchanged and agrees on the default (off).
Applies after speed-knobs-envs.patch (its lines are this patch's context):
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/int4-mq3d-envs.patch

--- a/envs.py
+++ b/envs.py
@@ -195,6 +195,9 @@
     VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE_DIR: str = ""
     VLLM_SPEC_DECODE_ATTN: bool = False
     VLLM_DRAFT_TOPK_TOPP: bool = True
+    # syv patch: int4 multi-query 3D verify switch and its debug print (same reason)
+    VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D: bool = False
+    VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D_DEBUG: bool = False
     # GiB of vision-tower weights to keep in pinned host memory; 0 disables.
     VLLM_VISION_CPU_OFFLOAD_GB: float = 0.0
     VLLM_HUMMING_MOE_GEMM_TYPE: Literal["indexed", "grouped", "auto"] | None = None
@@ -1541,6 +1544,8 @@
     "VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE_DIR": lambda: os.environ.get("VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE_DIR", ""),
     "VLLM_SPEC_DECODE_ATTN": lambda: os.environ.get("VLLM_SPEC_DECODE_ATTN", "0") == "1",
     "VLLM_DRAFT_TOPK_TOPP": lambda: os.environ.get("VLLM_DRAFT_TOPK_TOPP", "1") == "1",
+    "VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D": lambda: os.environ.get("VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D", "0") == "1",
+    "VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D_DEBUG": lambda: os.environ.get("VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D_DEBUG", "0") == "1",
     "VLLM_VISION_CPU_OFFLOAD_GB": lambda: float(
         os.environ.get("VLLM_VISION_CPU_OFFLOAD_GB", "0")
     ),
